A||||4||Motorhead||Codes 15 and 34||||1||
Z||000000||Motorhead||06-10-2000||12:11 PM||||<BR>This is a new set of codes on me.  Online service guide says 15 is coolant sensor.  34 is map sensor.<BR>Engine seems to be running very rich.  Smoke, smell and stumbling badly under all throttle conditions.  This engine has never had overheating problems.  Engine will not start at all now.  I'm guessing fouled plugs.  Headed out to pull them now.  Any thoughts other than just arbitrarilly changing sensors anyone?  Could one problem be causing another sensor that is reading correctly to trip a code?<BR>Thanks,<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000001||Motorhead||06-10-2000||02:32 PM||||Coolant sensor resistance is within specs.<BR>Plugs were badly fouled, installed new Bosch Platinums.<BR>Installed MAP sensor from my '84.<BR>Cleaned all connectors.<BR>Rechecked timing.<BR>Cleared the computer.<BR>Started fine, settled into a 900 RPM idle.<BR>Road tested good, no codes. Idling at around 1600 RPM after driving.  What's that all about?  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-10-2000||02:56 PM||||check the coolant sensor wiring and connections. if the circuit is damaged/loose it can do some pretty anoying things. drive it a couple days after resetting the ECM. it takes a few miles for the ECM to relearn everything.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Motorhead||06-10-2000||03:20 PM||||Thanks Ogre.  I'm going to take some time tomorrow and go through all the wireing and connectors.  Just did a complete rebuild last year and thought I checked everything.  Won't hurt to check again I suppose.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Styles||06-11-2000||11:25 PM||||Hey about the plugs being boosch platinum you will be replacing them soon again!bosch platinums the way the are made are not hot enouph for the rating of the fiero. Trust me I tried the same thing. well good luck||||reg||1
